## 1. Vulnerability Summary

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **CVE** | §*CVE Number*§ |
| **CVSS** | 9.3 (Critical) |
| **Affected** | sudo 1.9.14 → 1.9.17 (all p-revisions) |
| **Fixed** | sudo 1.9.17p1 |
| **Discoverer** | Rich Mirch, Stratascale CRU |
| **Type** | Local Privilege Escalation — no special sudoers entries required |
| **Root Cause** | sudo reads `/etc/nsswitch.conf` from attacker-controlled chroot directory before completing authorization, allowing arbitrary NSS shared library loading with root privileges |

## 2. Exploitation Mechanism

When `sudo -R /tmp/attacker_root <cmd>` executes:
1. sudo calls `chroot()` to the attacker-specified directory
2. While chrooted, sudo reads `/etc/nsswitch.conf` from inside the chroot
3. A crafted `nsswitch.conf` (e.g., `passwd: §*Generic Secret*§ forces sudo to load `libnss_woot1337.so.2`
4. The `__attribute__((constructor))` function in the malicious `.so` executes as root
5. A root shell is obtained

